  "title": "Directorate of Library Services (DLS) - Moshi Co-operative University",
  "text": "Directorate of Library Services (DLS) - Moshi Co-operative University Online Learning Management System Online Application System Online Journal System Helpdesk System Alumni Portal Staff Mail MUSARIS FAQ Home Departments/Units Department of Knowledge Management Department of Readers Service Archives Unit Library Services Research Areas E-Resources Subscribed E-Resource Free E-Resources Directorate Members Academic Staff Administrative Staff Online Learning Management System Online Application System Online Journal System Helpdesk System Alumni Portal Staff Mail MUSARIS FAQ Home Departments/Units Department of Knowledge Management Department of Readers Service Archives Unit Library Services Research Areas E-Resources Subscribed E-Resource Free E-Resources Directorate Members Academic Staff Administrative Staff Directorate of Library Services (DLS) \"Our main focus is to meet the information needs of the academic community\" Dr. Jaffar M. Ponera Senior Librarian Director of Library Services Email: jaffar.ponera@mocu.ac.tz Mobile: +255 716 641 808 Dear, our esteemed library users,\n                        It is my privilege to welcome you to our library website. I hope this website will provide you with valuable information on the availability, accessibility and utilisation of our library resources and services. The Moshi Co-operative University (MoCU) has two libraries, one located at the Main Campus in Moshi, and the other at the Kizumbi Institute of Cooperative and Business Education (KICoB) in Shinyanga. Our main focus is to meet the information needs of the academic community. At present our library’s physical collection is about 45,000 titles covering books, periodicals, manuals, and reference materials. Also, our libraries subscribe to several online databases.  Additionally, our libraries are equipped with modern facilities to enhance the acquisition, processing, storage, preservation, searching and retrieval of information.\n                        Please be informed that access to our library resources and services is open to students and all staff of MoCU as well as the general public. However, the latter can access our library resources and services through a special membership subscription. To enhance the steady utilisation of library resources and services, our libraries are managed by knowledgeable, skilled, methodical and dedicated library staff who are always happy to assist users in locating, retrieving and using information. Being an academic unit, our libraries are also responsible for teaching, researching and providing consultancy services in library and information science, information and knowledge management, information literacy, records and archives management and related fields.\n                        Kindly feel free to send us your comments and feedback about our services via dcla@mocu.ac.tz. We are always excited and happy to be part of your academic and research success. You are warmly welcome! Membership Repository Programmes Moshi Campus (MoCU Library) Weekdays in Semester: 08h30 – 22h00 Weekdays Off Semester: 08h30 – 15h30 Public Holiday: Closed Saturdays in Semester: 14h00 – 18h00 Sundays in Semester: 15h00 – 18h00 Weekends Off Semester: Closed 📌 The library closes from 18h00 – 19h30 on weekdays for supper. 📌 During university exams, the library extends opening hours by 1 hour. Shinyanga Campus (KICoB Library) Weekdays in Semester: 08h30 – 22h00 Weekdays Off Semester: 08h30 – 15h30 Public Holiday: Closed Saturdays in Semester: 15h30 – 22h00 Sundays in Semester: 15h30 – 22h00 Weekends Off Semester: Closed 📌 The library closes from 18h00 – 19h30 on weekdays for supper. 📌 During university exams, the library extends opening hours by 1 hour. OPAC Useful Links TLA TLSB IFLA COTUL SCECSAL COSTECH World Bank Library of Congress American Library Association Libguides Library policy and procedures Rules and Regulations of the library Archives policy Institutional repository policy Technical Manual Your trusted partner in academic excellence. Our University is dedicated to fostering creativity, innovation, and a passion for learning Contact Us Vice Chancellor 06 Sokoine Road, 25121 Mfumuni, P.O. Box 474, Moshi, Tanzania Tel: +255 27 2751833 info@mocu.ac.tz vc@mocu.ac.tz Quick Links TCDC HESLB NACTVET East African Community (EAC) Tanzania Commission for Universities (TCU) Ministry of Education, Science and Technology MoCU on Digital Platforms Disclaimer Privacy Policy Terms & Conditions Copyright Title Content here slot gacor hari ini link gacor PAKDE4D sesetoto bobatoto sesetoto https://www.scovillsgrill.com situs gacor bayi toto slot online slot bayitototisu.com roma77",
